        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8a01fda0-7d74-5845-ba59-762f86e2a5ca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Creature Comforts, Wallace and Gromit, Shaun the Sheep, Chicken Run, Rex the Runt, Cracking Contraptions, The Wrong Trousers, A Close Shave\n- People: Nick Park, Christopher Sadler\n- Concepts: stop motion clay animation, comedy mockumentary, Academy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Creature Comforts originated in 1989 as a British humorous animated short film and later became a stop motion clay animation comedy mockumentary franchise.\n- Creature Comforts matched animated zoo animals with a soundtrack of people talking about their homes to make the animals appear to be interviewed about their living conditions.\n- Nick Park was born on 6 December 1958 and is an English director, writer, and animator.\n- Nick Park is best known as the creator of Wallace and Gromit and Shaun the Sheep.\n- Nick Park received Academy Awards for Creature Comforts in 1989, The Wrong Trousers in 1993, A Close Shave in 1995, and another work in 2005, and he was nominated for the award six times in total.\n- Christopher Sadler is primarily known for his work on Wallace and Gromit, Chicken Run, Rex the Runt, Cracking Contraptions, Creature Comforts, and Shaun the Sheep.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "eae69ec0-773c-5c9b-a957-b1ba5e1e14c7",
        "text": "Page: Creature Comforts. Sentence: Creature Comforts is a stop motion clay animation comedy mockumentary franchise originating in a 1989 British humorous animated short film of the same name.\nPage: Creature Comforts. Sentence: The film matched animated zoo animals with a soundtrack of people talking about their homes, making it appear as if the animals were being interviewed about their living conditions.\nPage: Nick Park. Sentence: Nicholas Wulstan \"Nick\" Park, CBE (born 6 December 1958) is an English director, writer and animator best known as the creator of \"Wallace and Gromit\" and \"Shaun the Sheep\".\nPage: Nick Park. Sentence: Park has been nominated for an Academy Award a total of six times, and won four with \"Creature Comforts\" (1989), \"The Wrong Trousers\" (1993), \"A Close Shave\" (1995), and \"\" (2005).\nPage: Christopher Sadler. Sentence: He is primarily known for his work on \"Wallace and Gromit\", \"Chicken Run\", \"Rex the Runt\", \"Cracking Contraptions\", \"Creature Comforts\" and \"Shaun the Sheep\".",
